{
  "id": "f04",
  "rule": "the block renderer (/wp/v2/block-renderer/{name}, Part G b13, b14): WordPress's order of checks on the test block type qp-it/notice (the arguments with their defaults first, so no context=edit is 400 for every caller, with Allow only for a permitted one; the context and attributes checked before post_id; then the permission, edit_post on a given post above 0, else edit_posts; then the case-sensitive lookup, 404 block_invalid with Allow), a registered type's attributes (unknown ones refused, a type mismatch, a support's attribute accepted), anything for an unregistered type, the escaped rendering by GET and POST, a block hidden by metadata.blockVisibility false (and the string \"false\", which does not hide it), HEAD, _fields and OPTIONS, a query name beating the URL's; core/paragraph (static, 404 on both sides) and core/archives, which WordPress renders and QuarkPress does not register (D51)",
